<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ustaše</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1929">1929</a>–<a href="/years/1945">1945</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Ustasha, Ustaša</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ustaše were a Croatian fascist and ultranationalist movement founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ante-pavelic">Ante Pavelić</a> in 1929, which used terrorism against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yugoslavia">Yugoslav state</a>, including the assassination of King Alexander in 1934. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/axis-powers">Axis</a> invasion in April 1941 they ruled the Independent State of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a>, carrying out <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genocide">genocide</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbs">Serbs</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romani-people">Roma</a>, with the Jasenovac camp at its centre. The regime collapsed in May 1945.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ustase.jpg" alt="Ustaše" width="320" height="458" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nanin7 Original artist of the badge unknown · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Usta%C5%A1e_symbol.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
